module b3;

<*
 A ray in a shape's own frame, running from origin along translation, with max_fraction bounding
 how far along the cast looks. What that bound is measured in belongs to each cast: the solid and
 hollow sphere casts do not agree on it.
*>
struct RayCastInput {
    Vec3 origin;
    Vec3 translation;
    float max_fraction;
}

<*
 A convex proxy swept along translation in a shape's own frame, the shape cast's counterpart to
 RayCastInput. The proxy's points are borrowed for the duration of the call — see ShapeProxy.

 can_encroach is read only on box3d's first iteration, and takes effect only past two and three
 quarter linear slops of total radius. A sphere and a capsule lend their own radius to that sum
 where a hull, a mesh and a height field lend none.
*>
struct ShapeCastInput {
    ShapeProxy proxy;
    Vec3 translation;
    float max_fraction;
    bool can_encroach;
}

<*
 Whether every component is finite and max_fraction is at least zero and below box3d's huge bound,
 which scales with the length unit. It says nothing about whether the ray reaches anything: a zero
 translation passes, and so does a ray starting inside the shape it is cast at. The sphere,
 capsule and hull casts assert it, and this build compiles all three assertions out.
*>
extern fn bool RayCastInput.is_valid(&self) @cname("b3IsValidRay");

<*
 Raw local-space ray casts. Private because a miss comes back as a struct whose remaining fields
 are undefined — the mesh returns the input's own max_fraction in one of them — and the wrappers
 in src/cast.c3 turn a miss into a fault.
*>
extern fn CastOutput ray_cast_sphere_raw(Sphere* shape, RayCastInput* input) @cname("b3RayCastSphere") @private;
extern fn CastOutput ray_cast_hollow_sphere_raw(Sphere* shape, RayCastInput* input) @cname("b3RayCastHollowSphere") @private;
extern fn CastOutput ray_cast_capsule_raw(Capsule* shape, RayCastInput* input) @cname("b3RayCastCapsule") @private;
extern fn CastOutput ray_cast_compound_raw(CompoundData* shape, RayCastInput* input) @cname("b3RayCastCompound") @private;
extern fn CastOutput ray_cast_hull_raw(HullData* shape, RayCastInput* input) @cname("b3RayCastHull") @private;
extern fn CastOutput ray_cast_mesh_raw(Mesh* shape, RayCastInput* input) @cname("b3RayCastMesh") @private;
extern fn CastOutput ray_cast_height_field_raw(HeightFieldData* shape, RayCastInput* input) @cname("b3RayCastHeightField") @private;

<*
 Raw local-space shape casts. Private for the reason the raw ray casts are, and for one more: a
 proxy holding no points is read as though it held its first point rather than refused, so the
 answer looks ordinary while describing geometry the caller never named. The wrappers in
 src/cast.c3 check the proxy first.
*>
extern fn CastOutput shape_cast_sphere_raw(Sphere* shape, ShapeCastInput* input) @cname("b3ShapeCastSphere") @private;
extern fn CastOutput shape_cast_capsule_raw(Capsule* shape, ShapeCastInput* input) @cname("b3ShapeCastCapsule") @private;
extern fn CastOutput shape_cast_compound_raw(CompoundData* shape, ShapeCastInput* input) @cname("b3ShapeCastCompound") @private;
extern fn CastOutput shape_cast_hull_raw(HullData* shape, ShapeCastInput* input) @cname("b3ShapeCastHull") @private;
extern fn CastOutput shape_cast_mesh_raw(Mesh* shape, ShapeCastInput* input) @cname("b3ShapeCastMesh") @private;
extern fn CastOutput shape_cast_height_field_raw(HeightFieldData* shape, ShapeCastInput* input) @cname("b3ShapeCastHeightField") @private;

<*
 Raw overlap predicates. Private because a proxy holding no points is not refused: four kinds read
 it as though it held its first point, and the mesh and the height field answer from a stack buffer
 nothing wrote, so the result follows the caller's stray memory. The wrappers refuse it.
*>
extern fn bool overlap_sphere_raw(Sphere* shape, Transform transform, ShapeProxy* proxy) @cname("b3OverlapSphere") @private;
extern fn bool overlap_capsule_raw(Capsule* shape, Transform transform, ShapeProxy* proxy) @cname("b3OverlapCapsule") @private;
extern fn bool overlap_compound_raw(CompoundData* shape, Transform transform, ShapeProxy* proxy) @cname("b3OverlapCompound") @private;
extern fn bool overlap_hull_raw(HullData* shape, Transform transform, ShapeProxy* proxy) @cname("b3OverlapHull") @private;
extern fn bool overlap_mesh_raw(Mesh* shape, Transform transform, ShapeProxy* proxy) @cname("b3OverlapMesh") @private;
extern fn bool overlap_height_field_raw(HeightFieldData* shape, Transform transform, ShapeProxy* proxy) @cname("b3OverlapHeightField") @private;
